{"id":"c1e949fd2c59d899e8d0e9963b93cf37ccbd4938","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"c1e949fd2c59d899e8d0e9963b93cf37ccbd4938","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"man/ukify.xml","lines":["@@ -307,7 +307,8 @@","           a verbatim inline blob. They must be used together, and without specifying any other UKI section","           parameters. <command>ukify</command> will attach the pcrsig JSON blob to the UKI. This is useful","           in combination with <option>--policy-digest</option> to create a UKI and then sign the TPM2 policy","-          digests offline.</para>","+          digests offline. <option>--pcrsig=</option> may also be set with <varname>PCRSig=</varname> in the","+          <literal>[UKI]</literal> section of the configuration file.</para>"," ","           <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v258\"/></listitem>","         </varlistentry>","@@ -486,6 +487,19 @@","           <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v257\"/></listitem>","         </varlistentry>"," ","+        <varlistentry>","+          <term><varname>Firmware=<replaceable>DIR</replaceable>...</varname></term>","+          <term><option>--efifw=<replaceable>DIR</replaceable></option></term>","+","+          <listitem><para>Zero or more directories with UEFI firmware images. Each directory must contain","+          exactly one file. Each image is placed in a separate <literal>.efifw</literal> section, together","+          with the name of its directory as the firmware ID, which <literal>uefi-fw</literal> entries in the","+          <literal>.hwids</literal> section refer to with their <literal>fwid</literal> key. In the","+          configuration file, items are separated by whitespace.</para>","+","+          <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v258\"/></listitem>","+        </varlistentry>","+","         <varlistentry>","           <term><varname>Uname=<replaceable>VERSION</replaceable></varname></term>","           <term><option>--uname=<replaceable>VERSION</replaceable></option></term>","@@ -524,7 +538,9 @@","           specified, and there's exactly one","           <varname>PCRPublicKey=</varname>/<option>--pcr-public-key=</option> or","           <varname>PCRCertificate=</varname>/<option>--pcr-certificate=</option> argument, that key will be","-          used. Otherwise, the section will not be present.</para>","+          used. Otherwise, if there's exactly one","+          <varname>PCRPrivateKey=</varname>/<option>--pcr-private-key=</option> argument, the public key is","+          derived from it. Otherwise, the section will not be present.</para>"," ","           <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v253\"/></listitem>","         </varlistentry>","@@ -540,6 +556,35 @@","           <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v257\"/></listitem>","         </varlistentry>"," ","+        <varlistentry>","+          <term><varname>EFIArch=<replaceable>ARCH</replaceable></varname></term>","+          <term><option>--efi-arch=<replaceable>ARCH</replaceable></option></term>","+","+          <listitem><para>The EFI architecture of the stub, one of <literal>ia32</literal>,","+          <literal>x64</literal>, <literal>arm</literal>, <literal>aa64</literal>,","+          <literal>riscv32</literal>, <literal>riscv64</literal>, <literal>loongarch32</literal>, and","+          <literal>loongarch64</literal>. It selects the default stub and the default directory for the","+          <literal>.hwids</literal> section. If not specified, the architecture of the local machine is","+          used. On x86-64 machines with 32-bit firmware, as reported by","+          <filename>/sys/firmware/efi/fw_platform_size</filename>, <literal>ia32</literal> is used","+          instead.</para>","+","+          <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v253\"/></listitem>","+        </varlistentry>","+","+        <varlistentry>","+          <term><varname>Stub=<replaceable>STUB</replaceable></varname></term>","+          <term><option>--stub=<replaceable>STUB</replaceable></option></term>","+","+          <listitem><para>The path to the stub to build the UKI or addon from. If not specified,","+          <filename>/usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi/linux<replaceable>ARCH</replaceable>.efi.stub</filename> is","+          used for a UKI, and","+          <filename>/usr/lib/systemd/boot/efi/addon<replaceable>ARCH</replaceable>.efi.stub</filename> for an","+          addon, where <replaceable>ARCH</replaceable> is the EFI architecture.</para>","+","+          <xi:include href=\"version-info.xml\" xpointer=\"v253\"/></listitem>","+        </varlistentry>","+","         <varlistentry>","           <term><varname>PCRBanks=<replaceable>PATH</replaceable></varname></term>","           <term><option>--pcr-banks=<replaceable>PATH</replaceable></option></term>"],"additions":47,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"shell-completion/bash/systemd-detect-virt","lines":["@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ _systemd_detect_virt() {","     local i verb comps"," ","     local -A OPTS=(","-        [STANDALONE]='-h --help --version -c --container -v --vm -q --quiet --cvm","+        [STANDALONE]='-h --help --version -c --container -v --vm -r --chroot -q --quiet --cvm","                              --private-users --list --list-cvm'","     )"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/boot/chid.h","lines":["@@ -5,61 +5,6 @@"," "," #include \"../fundamental/chid.h\" /* IWYU pragma: export */"," ","-/* A .hwids PE section consists of a series of 'Device' structures. A 'Device' structure binds a CHID to some","- * resource, for now only Devicetree blobs. Designed to be extensible to other types of resources, should the","- * need arise. The series of 'Device' structures is followed by some space for strings that can be referenced","- * by offset by the Device structures. */","-","-enum {","-        DEVICE_TYPE_DEVICETREE = 0x1, /* A devicetree blob */","-        DEVICE_TYPE_UEFI_FW    = 0x2